<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31150" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nŏmos</span></b> 
		i, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>m.</i> (and nŏmus), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νομός</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A district, province, nome</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thebais dividitur in praefecturas oppidorum,
					quos nomos vocant, duodecim,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 9, 9, § 49</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">substituunt alios nomos, ut Heroopoliten,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
				ib.</span></i>
			 § 50.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In music, <i>a tune, air</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Ner. 20</span></i>.</div>
